# Codex CLI artifacts
.codex

# Python caches
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# OS / editor artifacts
.DS_Store
*.swp

# Claude Code per-cwd scheduled-tasks lockfile (runtime state, never commit).
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

# Agent worktrees. Claude Code checks a branch out here when a task runs in isolation, so
# the directory holds whole extra copies of this repository — transient tool state, exactly
# like __pycache__, and never something to commit.
#
# It is ignored because whole-tree checks were reading it and could not be trusted while it
# existed. `git ls-files --others --exclude-standard` reports each nested checkout as a
# single directory entry, which a caller expecting file paths then tries to open and dies
# on with IsADirectoryError. The privacy sweep walked into them and reported hundreds of
# violations out of those checkouts' own fixtures — a guard nobody can read is off.
# (The sweep also now skips untracked files outright; this rule is what keeps them out of
# a listing in the first place, and the two are not substitutes.)
.claude/worktrees/

# Claude Code's per-user local settings, written automatically beside the tracked
# settings.json and filled with absolute home-directory paths and per-machine permission
# grants. Every contributor to this repository is an agent user, so this is the likeliest
# accidental commit here — and its contents are precisely what the validator's privacy
# sweep exists to keep out of a published tree. Only the local override is ignored.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Playwright / web-verify + demo-video artifacts (heavy; reference by path/CI-URL,
# never commit — see web-verify and the v2 planning workflow).
#
# Scoped to the output directories on purpose. A bare `*.webm` / `*.vtt` / `*.srt` glob
# is exactly what skills/demo-video/SKILL.md warns against: a repo-wide media glob
# silently untracks legitimately committed video or
# caption assets elsewhere in the tree. Every artifact those skills produce already
# lands in one of the directories below, so nothing needs the broader form. Keep any
# new rule scoped to a directory.
test-results/
playwright-report/
trace.zip
*-trace.zip
web-verify-frames/
demo-video-output/
demo-video-frames/

# plan-run per-phase progress logs for a delegated phase (ephemeral observation only —
# never committed; see the Delegation section of skills/plan-run/SKILL.md).
plans/**/progress/

# Saved runtime transcripts. They must outlive a session, so they cannot simply be written
# to a temporary directory — but they are megabytes of one runtime's raw stream, they embed
# absolute temporary paths, and they are evidence rather than source.
plans/**/runs/

# Your own private identifiers — repo names, internal package scopes, scaffolding-script
# names — that the validator should flag if they appear in a skill. Never commit this: the
# whole point of the file is to hold names that must not be published, so a copy that ships
# leaks exactly what it exists to catch.
#
# This rule protects a file you CREATE. It does not untrack one already committed: git
# applies .gitignore to untracked paths only. That asymmetry is deliberate — a project that
# already tracks such a file goes on tracking it, while the copy you write in your own clone
# stays invisible to git. Verified in both directions before this line was written.
#
# Start from scripts/private-identifiers.txt.example.
scripts/private-identifiers.txt
